// Regression test (Issue #180 follow-up): a do-while's body must be a
// braced block, same as while/if/for -- `do` immediately followed by
// anything other than '{' must be rejected with "Expected '{' to open the
// do-block body.", not silently reinterpreted (e.g. as `do` followed by a
// bare `while` statement).
fn main(): int {
    do while (true) {
        return 0;
    }
    return 1;
}
